# Hermes Agent secrets for the PortPass Scout profile.
# Copy to %LOCALAPPDATA%\hermes\.env (native Windows). Names only here;
# values are typed by Antonio into that file, never pasted into chat or
# committed (PortPass rule 6).

# --- Model provider: pick ONE path -----------------------------------------
# Path A: Nous Portal subscription (no key; run `hermes setup --portal`)
# Path B: Anthropic API key, a NEW key made for Hermes (not the Vercel one)
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# Path C: OpenRouter
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# --- Control channel: Telegram ---------------------------------------------
# From @BotFather (/newbot). Treat as a password.
TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=
# Antonio's numeric Telegram user id (from @userinfobot). Comma-separate to add Adon.
TELEGRAM_ALLOWED_USERS=
# Set by /sethome in the chat; can also be pinned here.
# TELEGRAM_HOME_CHANNEL=

# --- Optional hard limit -----------------------------------------------------
# Off by default. apply.ps1 -StrictWrites writes this line for you. It limits
# write_file/patch to these roots. The Hermes home MUST be in the list or
# skills, memory and cron edits fail. Semicolon-separated on Windows. Scout
# reads the repo and does not write to it; only a builder profile would.
# HERMES_WRITE_SAFE_ROOT=C:\Users\<you>\Documents\PortPass-Scout;C:\Users\<you>\AppData\Local\hermes

# --- Optional, later --------------------------------------------------------
# GitHub token so `gh` and the skills hub are not rate-limited (repo scope only).
# GITHUB_TOKEN=
# Dashboard/API server, only if something else must call Hermes.
# API_SERVER_ENABLED=false
# API_SERVER_KEY=
